I've written the session plan: two task files and the issue responses are in session_plan/. The commit step didn't happen because session_plan/ is gitignored, so git add refused the files. The command in the instructions ends in || true, so I didn't force-add them. The files are on disk if the harness reads them from there.

Task 1 (product, self-driven): `/export` stops overwriting existing files. Right now handle_export writes over whatever is at the path with no check, and the default path is conversation.md. So running /export twice silently replaces the first export, and /export README.md would replace the user's README. Claude Code fixed the same bug on Nov 17. The task:
• Adds a --force flag, and refuses to write over an existing file without it, saying nothing was written.
• Tests that the command printed in the refusal parses back to the same path with --force set.
• Updates the help text and docs/src/usage/commands.md.
• Lists the other commands that write to a path the user names, and files one issue for any that also overwrite silently.

This slot avoids config and safety, which the trajectory says took most of the recent work.

Task 2 (product, backlog drain): `Fixes #1209`, Part of #1202. bash -c "kill -9 1" and sh -c "crontab -r" currently run with no warning under an always allow rule or --yes. The task makes the parse-tree pass read a literal -c body of a known shell as the commands it runs. It includes:
• A before/after verdict table for all 33 safety checks, posted on #1209 before any code changes.
• A census test that fails before the change, and a sabotage-and-restore check that it fails by name.
• A before/after run over the existing command corpus, naming every command that changes verdict.
• Retargeting the dead (#1196) link in docs/src/troubleshooting/safety.md:110 to #1210.

Why #1209 for the drain slot: it has one mechanism and a precise done-when. The other candidates aren't closable today:
• #1100 is blocked. I checked yoagent 0.27.9's MCP transport code and it still exposes no server process id, so yoyo has nothing to kill from a panic hook.
• #1186 and #1206 are waiting on upstream yoagent fixes.
• #1210 would loosen the detector across commands like ssh, docker exec and python -c, which needs more checking than one slot allows.

